    "narrative": "Our roster for today is headlined by **Geraldo Perdomo**, who earns the top efficiency score of 55.17 against Phillips. While the matchup against a right-hander typically suppresses upside for a switch-hitter, the favorable 4.33 xERA of the opposing starter provides enough cushion to leverage his elite speed, a critical necessity in our 5x5 build. **Taylor Ward** follows closely at 52.92. Despite a moderate challenge from Woo, **Taylor Ward** benefits from a massive park factor boost and his prime leadoff positioning, which provides the volume needed to capitalize on run-scoring opportunities. We are leaning heavily into these two to anchor our offensive output today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved our depth pieces, with no players outside the starting four hitting the threshold due to scheduled off-days for **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Lawrence Butler**, and others. While **Masyn Winn** (49.02) and **Gleyber Torres** (48.56) made the final cut, both operate in a high-risk zone as they face right-handed starters in Scott and Matthews, respectively. **Gleyber Torres** in particular is hampered by a significant platoon disadvantage, forcing a nearly 13% reduction in his raw projection. We are essentially betting on their volume and lineup security over pure statistical efficiency today. We remain cautious regarding the health of **Cal Raleigh** and **Will Smith**, both of whom remain sidelined, while keeping an eye on whether **Bryson Stott**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Matt Chapman**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, or **Drew Gilbert** might find better leverage in upcoming slates if our starters falter today.",
